INSERT INTO public.resource_memory (id, title, summary, resource_type, content, tree_path, last_modify, metadata_, embedding_config, summary_embedding, created_at, updated_at, is_deleted, _created_by_id, _last_updated_by_id, organization_id, user_id) VALUES ('res_YL99','Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA)','Email discussion regarding carton label requirements for CVS, involving procedural aspects of label handling and the implementation details. The communication includes the testing process and supply chain management, ensuring compliance with existing label standards and addressing process-related questions.','email','Ok Barry, thanks for the update  Sai karlaIT Implementation specialistIL, USA  |  CSTmobile:510 – 377 - 2611sai.karla@item.com  item.com   From: Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 17, 2025 6:15 PMTo: Sai Sathvik Karla <sai.karla@item.com>; Bill Solano <Bill.Solano@lumistella.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>; Charles Ruark <charles.ruark@lumistella.com>Cc: Implementation@item.com; wise support <wisesupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Hi Sai, CVS is almost completely shipped already.  These labels and the processes surrounding them, pallet level tare and such, are not new.  CVS should have been handled the same way it was in 2024.  I hope these were the labels that were used for shipping CVS and that the pallet level tare process was followed like last year. Thanks,  Barry VinotSupply Chain PlannerFrom: Sai Sathvik Karla <sai.karla@item.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 17, 2025 3:08 PMTo: Bill Solano <Bill.Solano@lumistella.com>; Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>; Charles Ruark <charles.ruark@lumistella.com>Cc: Implementation@item.com; wise support <wisesupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Hello Barry, Please find the attached labels for CVS retailer. Carton Label:  Note: The bottom of the label is displaying CVS1 because I changed the label code to print the carton label in the stage environment   Pallet label:  Sai karlaIT Implementation specialistIL, USA  |  CSTmobile:510 – 377 - 2611sai.karla@item.com  item.com   From: Bill Solano <Bill.Solano@lumistella.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 10, 2025 7:06 PMTo: Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com>; Sai Sathvik Karla <sai.karla@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>; Charles Ruark <charles.ruark@lumistella.com>Cc: Implementation@item.com; wise support <wisesupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) @Sai Sathvik Karla, CVS (23920) sales order SO214738 940 has been sent for testing CVS labels. See attached files as well. Thanks,  Bill SolanoSr. EDI Technical SpecialistFrom: Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 10, 2025 5:51 PMTo: Sai Sathvik Karla <sai.karla@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>; Charles Ruark <charles.ruark@lumistella.com>Cc: Implementation@item.com; wise support <wisesupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.com; Bill Solano <Bill.Solano@lumistella.com>Subject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Adding @Charles Ruark – Do you know how to trigger an order in the test system?  Barry VinotSupply Chain PlannerFrom: Sai Sathvik Karla <sai.karla@item.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 10, 2025 3:55 PMTo: Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>Cc: Implementation@item.com; wise support <wisesupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Hello Barry, Good Day, Can you please trigger the test order for the CVS retailer so we can test the label Sai karlaIT Implementation specialistIL, USA  |  CSTmobile:510 – 377 - 2611sai.karla@item.com  item.com   From: Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com> Sent: Monday, September 1, 2025 11:15 AMTo: Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>Cc: Implementation@item.com; wise support <wisesupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Hi Jennifer, The carton label for CVS does not have a SSCC-18 barcode.  It only has a UPC barcode. The pallet level tare label for CVS is the one that needs a SSCC-18 barcode and should scan for all quantities of product on the given pallets.  Each pallet requires two identical pallet level tare labels. Thanks,  Barry VinotSupply Chain PlannerFrom: Jennifer Kuo <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com> Sent: Friday, August 29, 2025 7:55 PMTo: Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>; Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com>Cc: implementation item <implementation@item.com>; Wise Support <WISEsupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Thank you. This is exactly what I was looking for! Jennifer KuoAccount Implementation Manager  |  IT - ImplementationCA, USA  |  PSTmobile: 657 – 705 - 7549jennifer.kuo@item.com  |  jennifer.kuo@unisco.com item.com  |  unisco.com From: Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com> Sent: Friday, August 29, 2025 4:43 PMTo: Jennifer Kuo <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com>Cc: implementation item <Implementation@item.com>; Wise Support <WISEsupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: RE: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Hi Jennifer, Note this label has not changed from the label we used in 2024 from the Morgan Lakes facility. CVS     Pierre PettigrewDistribution Manager3350 Riverwood Parkway SE, Suite 300 | Atlanta, GA 30339770‑701‑6157 x 9388  From: Jennifer Kuo <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com> Sent: Friday, August 29, 2025 7:26 PMTo: Pierre Pettigrew <pierre.pettigrew@lumistella.com>; Barry Vinot <Barry.Vinot@lumistella.com>Cc: implementation item <Implementation@item.com>; Wise Support <WISEsupport@unisco.com>; lumistella.alessandro@unisco.comSubject: [External] Unis-item / Carton Label Requirements for CVS (LUMISTELLA) Hello Pierre, Hello Barry: Would you please send us the latest carton label requirements for CVS?  While prepping DN-781794 to ship, the Alessanrdo team noted that the SSCC barcode was not part of the CVS template design (please see screenshot below).  We would like to make sure that all required elements are in place before printing out the carton labels. Looks like the barcode on the label is the UPC for the item. Thank you!!  Jennifer KuoAccount Implementation Manager  |  IT - ImplementationCA, USA  |  PSTmobile: 657 – 705 - 7549jennifer.kuo@item.com  |  jennifer.kuo@unisco.com item.com  |  unisco.com The information in this email and any files transmitted with it may include confidential information and are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom are addressed in the email. It is not the intention of CCA and B, LLC d/b/a The Lumistella Company (the “Company” or “The Lumistella Company”) to transmit trade secrets to unauthorized recipients. To the extent a Company trade secret has been so transmitted, it is inadvertent and strictly prohibited. Unauthorized review, forwarding, printing, copying, distribution, or use of any such information in this email is prohibited and may be unlawful. If you have received this emai