Jeszka, David E <David.Jeszka@diageo.com> Cc: Neff, Katie <Katie.Neff@diageo.com>; Tiszai, Ferenc <Ferenc.Tiszai@diageo.com>; EDI UNISCO <edi@unisco.com> Subject: 回复: Change to 947 Inventory Adjustment spec Hi Sandor, Thank you for your prompt response. From my understanding, both seem to move stock from Available to On-hold. The only difference I can see is that one applies from Any to Any, while the other is except for good to any. From the perspective of status and good type, it looks like 322 already includes 349. Could you please provide a bit more detail on the distinction between the two? Thank you. Sincerely, Mia Chen Beijing, CN Sr. EDI Engineer mia.chen@item.com www.item.com M: +1 626-781-6193 发件人: Kozma, Sandor E <Sandor.Kozma@diageo.com> 发送时间: 2025年9月18日 18:17 收件人: Mia Chen <mia.chen@item.com>; Harwood, Mark (Vendor-Company-204) <Mark.Harwood@diageo.com>; Jeszka, David E <David.Jeszka@diageo.com> 抄送: Neff, Katie <Katie.Neff@diageo.com>; Tiszai, Ferenc <Ferenc.Tiszai@diageo.com> 主题: RE: Change to 947 Inventory Adjustment spec @Mia Chen – The difference between the two is the location of the stock initially prior to being moved into quality inspection. You can of stock in wither unrestricted or on block prior to moving into quality inspection. Does this answer your question? @Jeszka, David E – Please feel free to add your thoughts. Thank you. Sandor Senior Business Analyst – Logistics & Customer Service 1-845-661-3863 – cell From: Mia Chen <mia.chen@item.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 17, 2025 11:42 PM To: Harwood, Mark (Vendor-Company-204) <Mark.Harwood@diageo.com> Cc: Jeszka, David E <David.Jeszka@diageo.com>; Kozma, Sandor E <Sandor.Kozma@diageo.com>; Neff, Katie <Katie.Neff@diageo.com>; Tiszai, Ferenc <Ferenc.Tiszai@diageo.com> Subject: 回复: Change to 947 Inventory Adjustment spec Hi Mark, Could you please elaborate on the difference between 322 and 349? They look include each other. Thank you. Sincerely, Mia Chen Beijing, CN Sr. EDI Engineer mia.chen@item.com www.item.com M: +1 626-781-6193 发件人: Harwood, Mark (Vendor-Company-204) <Mark.Harwood@diageo.com> 发送时间: 2025年9月17日 17:50 收件人: Mia Chen <mia.chen@item.com> 抄送: Jeszka, David E <David.Jeszka@diageo.com>; Kozma, Sandor E <Sandor.Kozma@diageo.com>; Neff, Katie <Katie.Neff@diageo.com>; Tiszai, Ferenc <Ferenc.Tiszai@diageo.com> 主题: Re: Change to 947 Inventory Adjustment spec Hi Mia I''m UK time, so not early. Re the 311, that was a late requirement because we had to change how we considered the packaging stock for the purposes of planning. Let''s exclude that for now given lack of time, we can try and come back to it later and see if there''s a way to automate. Thanks Mark From: Mia Chen <mia.chen@item.com> Sent: 17 September 2025 10:21 To: Harwood, Mark (Vendor-Company-204) <Mark.Harwood@diageo.com> Cc: Jeszka, David E <David.Jeszka@diageo.com>; Kozma, Sandor E <Sandor.Kozma@diageo.com>; Neff, Katie <Katie.Neff@diageo.com>; Tiszai, Ferenc <Ferenc.Tiszai@diageo.com> Subject: 回复: Change to 947 Inventory Adjustment spec External-Email: Be cautious of clicking any link or attachment unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. Hi Mark, Thank you for the updated spec. Shall we still confirm the adjustment scenarios with Ops team or Katie? Thank you. Sincerely, Mia Chen Beijing, CN Sr. EDI Engineer mia.chen@item.com www.item.com M: +1 626-781-6193 发件人: Harwood, Mark (Vendor-Company-204) <Mark.Harwood@diageo.com> 发送时间: 2025年9月17日 1:30 收件人: Mia Chen <mia.chen@item.com> 抄送: Jeszka, David E <David.Jeszka@diageo.com>; Kozma, Sandor E <Sandor.Kozma@diageo.com>; Neff, Katie <Katie.Neff@diageo.com>; Tiszai, Ferenc <Ferenc.Tiszai@diageo.com> 主题: Change to 947 Inventory Adjustment spec Hi Mia I have updated the spec to take account of the combination of Inventory Status and Goods Type in your system. Hopefully this makes sense, I have added some information to try and make it clearer. Dave, Sandor, the spreadsheet is here if any adjustments are needed while I''m away: IB Inventory Adjustments 947.xlsx ​Thanks Mark','["business", "internal_business_communication", "project_updates"]','{"timestamp": "2025-10-19T08:46:23.934222+00:00", "operation": "created"}','{}','{"embedding_endpoint_type": "openai", "embedding_endpoint": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-3-small", "embedding_dim": 1536, "embedding_chunk_size": 8191, "handle": null, "azure_endpoint": null, "azure_version": null, "azure_deployment": null}','[-0.009785015,-0.004305135,-0.016052585,-0.040769763,-0.024581369,0.03338177,-0.024391238,0.011149892,0.003524235,-0.03129032,-0.0047023753,-0.00088360516,-0.0029470483,-0.0012604742,-0.007815789,0.008542365,0.021960262,0.01518341,0.0043390873,-0.015563674,-0.022747952,0.019176185,-0.00829112,0.02819388,-0.023114637,-0.016799534,0.016174814,-0.005449323,-0.01739709,0.01488463,-0.002778985,0.0073336684,-0.019991037,0.0047533037,-0.01708473,-0.043187156,0.0021967052,-0.041448805,0.025790067,-0.028411174,0.01751932,0.01646001,0.0066376487,-0.016079746,-0.0064101694,0.018130457,-0.0005211658,0.008868306,0.0025939457,0.011183844,0.03085573,0.00939117,-0.0166094,-0.012895034,-0.010185651,-0.007374411,0.011584479,0.0011034454,-0.010009099,-0.007870113,-0.006447517,-0.025504868,-0.022163976,0.016188394,-0.022693628,0.00045580787,-0.003693996,-0.0067700623,0.024717178,0.0037381337,0.052041885,0.020126846,0.003602325,-0.01986881,0.020792307,-0.0031117161,0.012949357,-0.008718917,0.0038875232,0.013906808,0.021417027,-0.015631579,-0.01690818,0.023915907,0.0053610476,0.015631579,0.002531134,0.019692257,-0.00845409,0.011353605,0.0026295953,0.009594883,0.0019301807,0.013485801,-0.021525675,0.0027823802,0.0033137316,0.034386758,0.015699483,-0.015876034,-0.014680917,0.013662352,-0.024092458,-0.0035412111,-0.023481319,-0.009947985,0.008956582,-0.017329186,-0.020629337,0.008949791,-0.0310187,0.019135442,0.013261717,-0.01675879,0.024201106,0.024961634,0.019665096,-0.0095337685,-0.006953404,-0.030964378,-0.0067