INSERT INTO public.resource_memory (id, title, summary, resource_type, content, tree_path, last_modify, metadata_, embedding_config, summary_embedding, created_at, updated_at, is_deleted, _created_by_id, _last_updated_by_id, organization_id, user_id) VALUES ('res_VA42','Weekly Report (20250915-20250919)','Email from Eaden Wu to Shelia Sun containing detailed weekly project status updates and customer interactions from 2025-09-15 to 2025-09-19. Covers various customer accounts, integration progress, system configurations, and specific tasks completed within the week.','email','Dear All, 周报内容如下，祝周末愉快! DATE 9/20/2025 WEEKLY REPORT To:Shelia Sun From:Eaden WU Subject:Weekly Project Status Update Period Ending:9/15 – 9/19 ACTIVITIES IN THIS WEEK ACTIVITIES IN PROCESS NEXT ACTION Name: Eaden’ Customers:TCL NORTH AMERICA, EMS MIND READER LLC ,MIKE''S HOT HONEY, SharkNinja Sales Company, EMS MIND READER LLC,VITA COCO - DTC, FILIPPO BERIO USA LTD, MONSTER ENERGY COMPANY, DEER STAGS, KARAKA, LLC, LLC, Flowserve , Angelcare, 5 Star Apparel LLC Tasks and Incidents for Customers After Go-Live TCL NORTH AMERICA —Ongoing-Assisted the customer in enabling the new warehouse El Paso/Riverside inventory report. The daily inventory has now been restored, and the data has been confirmed as normal. -Assisted the customer in handling a DC exception. Upon confirmation, the issue was due to the WMS 3.0 system not enforcing the rule that Carrier SCAC length must be four characters. A ticket has been submitted to align with the WMS 2.0 logic. -Assisted the customer in troubleshooting missing DCs for order shipments. It was confirmed that during warehouse fulfillment, multiple SKUs were placed on the same pallet, causing DC validation to fail. We are currently waiting for the customer to confirm whether mixed-pallet scenarios are involved, and how DCs should be provided in such cases. EMS MIND READER LLC —Done-Assisted internal team in completing the Preview environment, organizing and importing 21 order records, and verifying that the DCs met expectations. -Assisted internal team in adjusting the Retailer = ODC2 Packing List mapping logic, verifying Packing List printing in both production and test environments, and synchronizing the configuration code between the two environments. SharkNinja Sales Company —Done-Assisted the customer in investigating the EDI_940 issue, where the second batch of imported orders did not update the Carrier SCAC and LoadNo information. After verification, it was confirmed that WMS had already created the loads, but the carriers were not activated, which caused the data not to be updated. The data has now been remapped. -Collaborated with the customer to adjust the mapping logic for Retailer=SAM CLUBS and generated test files in the Stage environment for verification. The customer has confirmed that the tests passed, and the change has now been deployed to the production environment. VITA COCO - DTC —Ongoing-The EDI_846 inventory logic has been adjusted, and all warehouse reports have been enabled. No exceptions have been reported by the customer so far, moving to Done. MONSTER ENERGY COMPANY —Done- Assisted the customer in identifying the cause of the EDI_940 import issue and confirmed that it was due to missing ShipToCity and ShipToZipCode information, which caused internal DN interface calls to fail. The customer has now successfully imported the orders via ClientPortal, and has been reminded to provide complete data in the future. DEER STAGS —Done- Assisted the customer in identifying the cause of the RC data issue. The RC data failed to be sent due to an exception in the WMS interface. The issue has been flagged for correction, and the data has been successfully resent. KARAKA, LLC —Done- The customer reported that inventory reports generated from different warehouses have different structures. After verification, it was confirmed that the customer’s ValleyView warehouse has been upgraded to WMS 3.0, which is not consistent with the inventory report interface from WMS 2.0. A ticket has been submitted for a fix, and we are waiting for the ETA. New Customer Overview #1 Customer Name (Mandatory): CubeShip-VIZIO 1) Integration Progress Detailed status of ongoing integration efforts (Mandatory) Continuing to support the customer in testing ASN messages, we are waiting for the CubeShip team to adjust the BSN/REF segment date information as requested by the customer and regenerate the ASN for transmission. 2) Labels/BOL/Packing List(printing Docs) Docs Counts (Mandatory)：0 Associated Jira Tickets & Stuck Points (Optional) Status Descriptions (Mandatory) Null Current Challenges and Blockers (Optional) 3) Wise System Configuration Detailed description of Wise setup activities (Mandatory) The customer already exists, no configuration is needed. 4) Customized Requirements Jira Tickets & Blockers (Optional) Specific customizations and implementation notes (Optional) 5) Item Master Preview Imports (Mandatory) The customer already exists, no configuration is needed. Production Imports (Mandatory) The customer already exists, no configuration is needed. Special Requirements (Mandatory) Null 6) Shipping Accounts Small Parcel Account Setup (Mandatory) Null Shipping Routing Table (Optional) Billing Party Setup (Optional) 7) Retailers Configuration of retailer profiles within Wise (Mandatory) The customer already exists, no configuration is needed. 8) Other Summary of overall issues, blockers, and unresolved problems (Optional) #2 Customer Name (Mandatory): Angelcare 1) Integration Progress Detailed status of ongoing integration efforts (Mandatory) Continuing to assist the customer with EDI_940/945 testing. The second round of EDI_940/945 testing has been completed, and we are preparing to test and verify in the production environment. 2) Labels/BOL/Packing List(printing Docs) Docs Counts (Mandatory)：0 Associated Jira Tickets & Stuck Points (Optional) Status Descriptions (Mandatory) Null Current Cha