INSERT INTO public.resource_memory (id, title, summary, resource_type, content, tree_path, last_modify, metadata_, embedding_config, summary_embedding, created_at, updated_at, is_deleted, _created_by_id, _last_updated_by_id, organization_id, user_id) VALUES ('res_KZ7J','OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC Order Processing Exceptions','Email chain detailing the order processing exceptions detected in OMS for ADOORN LLC, including discussions on handling insufficient inventory and the steps required to update orders in Wise and manage exceptions. Provides a comprehensive view of problem-solving approaches and decision-making processes.','email','Hi @Laurel Weissman,The exception orders history has been cleaned. Please check the order statuses when you have a chance — they should now be visible in Wise. However, there are still some orders in exception due to insufficient inventory of DS-4MHN-SILVER-1. If you’d like the orders with available inventory to flow into our system, please update the affected orders. Alternatively, we can wait until your inventory is replenished and then release all orders together, which may help reduce manual effort on your side. If you’d prefer us to handle exception orders daily, please let us know, and we’ll proceed with a daily cleanup after your update. Thanks! Best Regards, Juan Dai (Livia) Beijing, China IT Implementation/EDI Engineer Email: livia.dai@item.com From: Laurel Weissman <laurel@adoorn.com> Sent: Monday, September 15, 2025 20:12 To: Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> Cc: Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil <cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com>; Implementation@item.com <Implementation@item.com>; Cara Gao <cara.gao@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; adam@nxtascent.com <adam@nxtascent.com>; adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com <adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com>; adoorn.innovation@unisco.com <adoorn.innovation@unisco.com>; Mallory Tessler <mallory@adoorn.com>; Mail Service <mail.service@item.com> Subject: Re: 【OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC 】 Order Processing Exceptions Detected – Action Required Hi Livia, We finished this effort Friday, please have your developers import the updated orders. This is something we will likely need to do daily to keep things moving until the inventory is back in stock. Thank you, Laurel Laurel Weissman Inventory & Operations Manager 312-776-3347 | www.adoorn.com | laurel@adoorn.com 651 W Washington Blvd., Ste 301 Chicago, IL 60661 On Sun, Sep 14, 2025 at 8:40 PM Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> wrote: Hi @Laurel Weissman, If you decide to import the updated order and create separate orders for the out-of-stock item DS-4MHN-SILVER-1, the rest of the items in the order can be fulfilled as normal. The out-of-stock item orders will be fulfilled once inventory becomes available. Please let me know when you finished update the Shopify orders by removing DS-4MHN-SILVER-1. At that point, I can have our developer clear the exception history so we can pull the updated orders. Otherwise, the updated orders will not be imported into our system. Thanks! Best Regards, Juan Dai (Livia) Beijing, China IT Implementation/EDI Engineer Email: livia.dai@item.com From: Laurel Weissman <laurel@adoorn.com> Sent: Saturday, September 13, 2025 2:51 To: Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> Cc: Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil <cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com>; Implementation@item.com <Implementation@item.com>; Cara Gao <cara.gao@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; adam@nxtascent.com <adam@nxtascent.com>; adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com <adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com>; adoorn.innovation@unisco.com <adoorn.innovation@unisco.com>; Mallory Tessler <mallory@adoorn.com>; Mail Service <mail.service@item.com> Subject: Re: 【OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC 】 Order Processing Exceptions Detected – Action Required Thank you for explaining. We are going to update the order in Shopify and REMOVE the DS-4MHN-SILVER-1 from the order. The expectation is the order will re-import in 4 hours and process regularly. We will create a new order in shopify, just for the OOS item and expect that to sit in this report until the inventory arrives. Please advise ASAP if you see anything wrong with this plan. We are working to get this inventory replenished next week. Thank you, Laurel Laurel Weissman Inventory & Operations Manager 312-776-3347 | www.adoorn.com | laurel@adoorn.com 651 W Washington Blvd., Ste 301 Chicago, IL 60661 On Fri, Sep 12, 2025 at 11:31 AM Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> wrote: Hi @Laurel Weissman, Please see my answers below for your reference: - The orders in this report, since these are not in Wise the inventory has not been committed, correct? This would be for any item on the orders. Yes, no inventory in the order has been committed, and this applies to all items within the order. - Are you saying tracking will not go back for any item and any point of fulfillment? All tracking would be manually loaded? If you decide to short ship and manually create the backorder, then no tracking will be sent back automatically. You would need to manually upload the tracking information to Shopify. Thanks! Best Regards, Juan Dai (Livia) Beijing, China IT Implementation/EDI Engineer Email: livia.dai@item.com From: Laurel Weissman <laurel@adoorn.com> Sent: Saturday, September 13, 2025 0:22 To: Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> Cc: Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil <cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com>; Implementation@item.com <Implementation@item.com>; Cara Gao <cara.gao@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; adam@nxtascent.com <adam@nxtascent.com>; adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com <adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com>; adoorn.innovation@unisco.com <adoorn.innovation@unisco.com>; Mallory Tessler <mallory@adoorn.com>; Mail Service <mail.service@item.com> Subject: Re: 【OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC 】 Order Processing Exceptions Detected – Action Required Hi Livia - Thank you, we are aware we are out of stock on the DS-4MHN-SILVER-1, we are working to remedy that. A couple points to confirm: - The orders in this report, since these are not in Wise the inventory has not been committed, correct? This would be for any item on the orders. - Are you saying tracking will not go back for any item and any point of fulfillment? All tracking would be manually loaded? This will help our team decide how to handle. Thank you, Laurel Weissman Inventory & Operations Manager 312-776-3347 | www.adoorn.com | laurel@adoorn.com 651 W Washington Blvd., Ste 301 Chicago, IL 60661 On Fri, Sep 12, 2025 at 11:15 AM Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> wrote: Hi @Laurel Weissman, I randomly checked some orders and found that the exception was caused by no inventory for item DS-4MHN-SILVER-1. Please note that when any item in an order is out of stock, the entire order will fail to import. If you would like the order to be short shipped, the tracking information will not flow back to Shopify since the shipped quantities would not match the original order, which is treated as a modification. In this case, you would need to manually update all tracking numbers. Regarding backorders, our system does not create them automatically. If you need backorders placed, they must be created through the client portal or by contacting our warehouse operations team. The tracking numbers for backorders would also need to be manually updated. For these reasons, we generally do not recommend short shipping and creating backorders, as it can add significant complexity. However, if you would like the orders to be processed quickly and are comfortable with the extra steps, I can release them for you. Alternatively, I can import the orders into WISE and let them remain in exception status until all items are back in stock, at which point they can be processed in full, rather than staying in OMS and continuing to appear on your exception reports. Thanks! Best Regards, Juan Dai (Livia) Beijing, China IT Implementation/EDI Engineer Email: livia.dai@item.com From: Laurel Weissman <laurel@adoorn.com> Sent: Friday, September 12, 2025 23:50 To: Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> Cc: Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil <cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com>; Implementation@item.com <Implementation@item.com>; Cara Gao <cara.gao@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; adam@nxtascent.com <adam@nxtascent.com>; adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com <adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com>; adoorn.innovation@unisco.com <adoorn.innovation@unisco.com>; Mallory Tessler <mallory@adoorn.com>; Mail Service <mail.service@item.com> Subject: Re: 【OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC 】 Order Processing Exceptions Detected – Action Required see attached. Laurel Weissman Inventory & Operations Manager 312-776-3347 | www.adoorn.com | laurel@adoorn.com 651 W Washington Blvd., Ste 301 Chicago, IL 60661 On Fri, Sep 12, 2025 at 10:48 AM Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com> wrote: Hi @Laurel Weissman, Could you please share the list with us? Thanks! Best Regards, Juan Dai (Livia) Beijing, China IT Implementation/EDI Engineer Email: livia.dai@item.com From: Laurel Weissman <laurel@adoorn.com> Sent: Friday, September 12, 2025 23:14 To: Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil <cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com> Cc: Implementation@item.com <Implementation@item.com>; Cara Gao <cara.gao@item.com>; Livia Dai <livia.dai@item.com>; Jennifer Kuo - Unisco <jennifer.kuo@unisco.com>; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; adam@nxtascent.com <adam@nxtascent.com>; adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com <adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com>; adoorn.innovation@unisco.com <adoorn.innovation@unisco.com>; Mallory Tessler <mallory@adoorn.com>; Mail Service <mail.service@item.com> Subject: Re: 【OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC 】 Order Processing Exceptions Detected – Action Required Hello, Following up on this request to better understand this list, so we can help resolve orders not processing. Thank you, Laurel Laurel Weissman Inventory & Operations Manager 312-776-3347 | www.adoorn.com | laurel@adoorn.com 651 W Washington Blvd., Ste 301 Chicago, IL 60661 On Wed, Sep 10, 2025 at 11:25 AM Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil <cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com> wrote: Hi @implementation item / @Cara Gao / @Jennifer Kuo / @Livia Dai / @Alfred Garcia Please advise. Thank you! Best Regards, Cleo Ivonne Bongcawil UF – Client Support Phone: +19096551024 Email: cleo.bongcawil@unisco.com Facility: 6800 Valley View St. Buena Park, CA 90620 Website: www.unisco.com NOTICE: This message, and any attachments, contain(s) information that may be confidential or protected by privilege from disclosure and is intended only for the individual or entity named above. No one else may disclose, copy, distribute, or use the contents of this message for any purpose. Its unauthorized use, dissemination, or duplication is strictly prohibited and may be unlawful. If you receive this message in error or you otherwise are not an authorized recipient, please immediately delete the message and any attachments and notify the sender. From: Laurel Weissman <laurel@adoorn.com> Sent: Wednesday, September 10, 2025 9:16 AM To: mail.service@item.com Cc: adam@nxtascent.com; adoorn.seabrook@unisco.com; adoorn.innovation@unisco.com; Cara Gao <Cara.gao@item.com>; Mallory Tessler <mallory@adoorn.com> Subject: Re: 【OMS Prod Alert-ADOORN LLC 】 Order Processing Exceptions Detected – Action Required Hello, I need help understanding this report. Does this mean the following entire orders are not being imported? What is the SKU or SKUs impacting this? We are currently out of DS-4MHN-SILVER-1 at both locations and those orders can short ship and a back order be created for that item. Please advise so I can determine any needed instructions. Thank you, Laurel Laurel Weissman Inventory & Operations Manager 312-776-3347 | www.adoorn.com | laurel@adoorn.com 651 W Washington Blvd., Ste 301 Chicago, IL 60661 On Wed, Sep 10, 2025 at 11:00 AM mail.service@item.com <mail.service@item.com> wrote: Dear User, Our system has detected the following exceptions during order creation or dispatch processing. Please review and resolve them as soon as possible to avoid any delays or data issues. Please log in to the OMS system to handle the above exceptions. If you need assistance, contact your system administrator or support team. Thank you for your cooperation. Best regards, OMS Notification Center','["Internal Business Communication", "Project Updates"]','{"timestamp": "2025-10-19T15:54:35.917095+00:00", "operation": "created"}','{}','{"embedding_endpoint_type": "openai", "embedding_endpoint": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-3-small", "embedding_dim": 1536, "embedding_chunk_size": 8191, "handle": null, "azure_endpoint": null, "azure_version": null, "azure_deployment": null}','[-0.010798908,-0.016430672,-0.015248002,-0.032382645,-0.026807196,0.026905753,-0.016191322,-0.013319122,-0.008771473,-0.013417678,0.00029082783,-0.02172453,-0.018838251,0.01502273,-0.010186453,0.0016182523,0.024653047,-0.018542582,-0.00812382,-0.0035163327,-0.034522712,-0.01552959,-0.005279779,0.0004936593,0.015557748,0.0012601072,0.01265035,-0.024976874,-0.012664429,-0.017007926,0.023414059,0.00094068056,-0.00033724587,-0.009081219,-0.0116929505,0.014234284,0.0029478765,-0.014170926,0.0043047797,-0.02628626,0.045392018,0.0070749037,0.0112846475,0.0029848348,0.0003269063,0.018697457,0.0035849698,0.007342412,-0.0051741833,-0.004702523,-0.0012099493,0.0190776,-0.014375078,-0.0041147075,0.027398532,0.024174348,0.006733478,0.0027384453,-0.011129773,-0.0116929505,-0.013220566,0.00667716,-0.027257739,0.017458469,-0.022470739,0.009038981,-0.029876508,0.011608474,0.011671831,-0.023695648,0.0410274,0.007933748,-0.033114772,0.0013894618,0.030580478,-0.023568932,-0.006958748,0.022935359,0.00549449,-0.0038999966,0.0012354682,-0.008630678,-0.013706306,0.018331392,0.0018602421,0.012347642,0.010615875,0.009355768,-0.0064589293,0.010700352,0.011467679,0.041168194,0.0128615415,0.004322379,-0.012340602,0.013945656,-0.006846113,0.04156242,-