2025-10-19 16:51:06.026493+00','2025-10-19 16:51:06.032753+00','false',NULL,NULL,'org-00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000','user-43a92772-e76b-4e5d-a1bd-3d32992580f9');
INSERT INTO public.resource_memory (id, title, summary, resource_type, content, tree_path, last_modify, metadata_, embedding_config, summary_embedding, created_at, updated_at, is_deleted, _created_by_id, _last_updated_by_id, organization_id, user_id) VALUES ('res_GT96','Incorrect Ship ID Discussion','Email thread discussing updates and corrections regarding shipment IDs and BOLs for GNC orders, involving multiple stakeholders.','email','Hi Pearlyn,This is noted on our end. Our team will monitor the next GNC shipments to ensure that ASNs have the correct shipment ID.Thank you.Regards,Johanna Marie SarmientoRetail/Offline Operationsjohanna@goessor.comgoessor.comLinkedinOn Thu, Sep 11, 2025 at 3:42 AM Pearlyn Villarin <pearlyn.villarin@unisco.com> wrote:Hello @Johanna,The order DN-2720431 was received with a shipment ID of 200201 when our team received the routing. The “_SP” suffix was added to the shipment ID or load number as an internal measure to indicate that a BOL had been attached to the order. This was done to ensure that the correct BOL was used, rather than using UNIS BOL.Previously, for GNC routings, no BOLs were attached, and we used the UNIS BOL by default. However, with recent changes, we are now receiving BOLs along with the routing information.That said, this has now been addressed on our end. Going forward, all GNC orders will no longer include the "_SP" suffix on the shipment ID or load number. Please note that this change only applies to the GNC retailer.Let me know if you have any questions.Thank you,Pearlyn VillarinUF Client Support Team Lead Phone: 310.747.7444Email: pearlyn.villarin@unisco.comFacility: 218 Machlin Ct., Walnut, CA 91789Website: www.unisco.com From: Pearlyn Villarin <pearlyn.villarin@unisco.com> Sent: Tuesday, September 9, 2025 11:07 AMTo: Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; Johanna Marie Sarmiento <johanna@goessor.com>; heyday.bp@unisco.comCc: Rajan MEC <rajan.bt@mobilityecommerce.ai>; Pierre Leblanc <pierre.l@goessor.com>; Laurel Custer <Laurel-Custer@gnc-hq.com>; tomas@goessor.com; SC Wholesale <scwholesale@goessor.com>; Aly LaBonne <aly.labonne@goessor.com>; EDI ITEM <edi@item.com>Subject: RE: Incorrect Ship ID Hello @Johanna, Will check on our end and will provide an update once we have all the information needed.Thank you,Pearlyn VillarinUF Client Support Team Lead Phone: 310.747.7444Email: pearlyn.villarin@unisco.comFacility: 218 Machlin Ct., Walnut, CA 91789Website: www.unisco.com From: Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com> Sent: Tuesday, September 9, 2025 11:00 AMTo: Johanna Marie Sarmiento <johanna@goessor.com>; heyday.bp@unisco.comCc: Rajan MEC <rajan.bt@mobilityecommerce.ai>; Pierre Leblanc <pierre.l@goessor.com>; Laurel Custer <Laurel-Custer@gnc-hq.com>; tomas@goessor.com; SC Wholesale <scwholesale@goessor.com>; Aly LaBonne <aly.labonne@goessor.com>; EDI ITEM <edi@item.com>Subject: RE: Incorrect Ship ID Hi @HEYDAY.BP@unisco.com, Please review the customer''s inquiry below regarding how the shipment ID or load ID name/number is generated and determined in the system. Regards,Alfred GarciaEDI AnalystBuena Park, CA | PSTalfred.garcia@item.com | www.item.com From: Johanna Marie Sarmiento <johanna@goessor.com> Sent: Tuesday, September 9, 2025 7:01 AMTo: Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; HEYDAY.BP@unisco.comCc: Rajan MEC <rajan.bt@mobilityecommerce.ai>; Pierre Leblanc <pierre.l@goessor.com>; Laurel Custer <Laurel-Custer@gnc-hq.com>; tomas@goessor.com; SC Wholesale <scwholesale@goessor.com>; Aly LaBonne <aly.labonne@goessor.com>; edi <edi@item.com>Subject: Re: Incorrect Ship ID @HEYDAY.BP@unisco.com From the screenshot of the order (DN-2720431) that Alfred provided, could you confirm that "200201" is the Shipment ID you received from Manhattan? If yes, @Alfred Garcia where does _SP BOL come from?@Rajan MEC Regards,Johanna Marie SarmientoRetail/Offline Operationsjohanna@goessor.comgoessor.comLinkedin On Tue, Sep 9, 2025 at 7:34 AM Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com> wrote:Hi @Johanna Marie Sarmiento/@Rajan MEC, N9_BM à BOLN9_CN à tracking numberN9_RU à Load ID / shipment ID Regards,Alfred GarciaEDI AnalystBuena Park, CA | PSTalfred.garcia@item.com | www.item.com From: Johanna Marie Sarmiento <johanna@goessor.com> Sent: Sunday, September 7, 2025 11:26 PMTo: Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>Cc: Pierre Leblanc <pierre.l@goessor.com>; Laurel Custer <Laurel-Custer@gnc-hq.com>; tomas@goessor.com; SC Wholesale <scwholesale@goessor.com>; Aly LaBonne <aly.labonne@goessor.com>; edi <edi@item.com>; Rajan MEC <rajan.bt@mobilityecommerce.ai>Subject: Re: Incorrect Ship ID @Alfred Garcia Can you pls check this on your end? Thanks On Sat, Sep 6, 2025 at 12:26 AM Rajan MEC <rajan.bt@mobilityecommerce.ai> wrote:Pierre,The SHIP ID, is received in 945 from UNIS, so they need to check what they send for this particular issue. Can you check with UNIS, which qualifier is the required data they are sending, so that we can map it accordingly. Rajan On Fri, 5 Sept 2025 at 17:30, Pierre Leblanc <pierre.l@goessor.com> wrote:Hi @Rajan MEC , Following up on this message. Could you review the GNC EDI 856 mapping and tell us which field from the EDI 945 is used for ShipID ?Thank you,Pierre On Fri, Aug 29, 2025 at 10:12 AM Pierre Leblanc <pierre.l@goessor.com> wrote:Hello @Rajan MEC , Could you share with Alfred which field from the EDI 945 is Mobility using as ShipID on EDI 856 ? Thank you,Pierre On Fri, Aug 29, 2025 at 1:06 AM Johanna Marie Sarmiento <johanna@goessor.com> wrote:@Pierre Leblanc @Rajan MEC Could you check? Thank you. On Fri, Aug 29, 2025 at 4:36 AM Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com> wrote:Hi @Johanna Marie Sarmiento, Kindly confirm which field in the 945 you are pulling the ship ID information for us to update our map solely for GNC. Thank you! Regards,Alfred GarciaEDI AnalystBuena Park, CA | PSTalfred.garcia@item.com | www.item.com From: Johanna Marie Sarmiento <johanna@goessor.com> Sent: Thursday, August 28, 2025 12:32 PMTo: Laurel Custer 