It seems you guys are working hard to get this shipping and reporting issue resolved but despite the hard work nothing seems to be changing. We have repeatedly communicated to our CEO and CMO that we will be on track in the next few hours… which has now turned into 5 days. Friday night we were told we would have everything shipped – it wasn’t –a new problem was discovered. We thought the team would be shipping on Sunday – It didn’t – no one told us we weren’t set up for weekend shipping. We thought everything would be fixed (shipped and transactions flowing to Amazon) Monday mid-afternoon – it wasn’t. We expected to see orders moving by Tuesday AM – They didn’t. We expected to see this resolved this afternoon – it hasn’t.

Are we getting the full story about the issues? Are you comfortable that UNIS can handle the Ready® Amazon business? If not we should understand that quickly so we do not see further erosion to our Amazon business and can make different arrangements.

I really don’t understand how every part of this process failed!

Who on the UNIS management team is aware of this failed go live, the problems resolving the issues, and the harm this is doing to the Ready Amazon business.

We have already had over 100 orders cancelled in the past few days and expect more cancellations as this issue continues be unresolved.

Mark, what is the plan to get this resolved?

How can I help?

Christopher Nettleton
Chief Financial Officer
Ready®
170 Church Road, Wexford, PA 15090
412.939.3399 – Office
412.477.4355 – Cell
Cnettleton@teamready.com
www.teamready.com

From: Michael Deller <mdeller@teamready.com>
Sent: Tuesday, September 9, 2025 6:38 PM
To: Melissa Ortiz <melissa.ortiz@unisco.com>
Cc: comeready.bp@unisco.com; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; Steven Garcia <steven.garcia@unisco.com>; Mark Golding <mark.golding@unisco.com>; Chris Nettleton <cnettleton@teamready.com>
Subject: RE: COME READY OPEN ORDERS 9/9

Melissa,
This is a nice informational status grid. Thanks for pulling it together. But it is not updating me on why only 19 boxes have left the building out of 716 to be shipped. The only update below is IT is still working on an issue on the orders with beverage. From my quick look in pic below, that is only around 300 of the total orders (I filtered down to count orders with beverage). So if the beverage is the only pending glitch, why aren’t 300 other boxes out the door by now?

It feels like there is something much larger going on here on the system/IT side that nobody is telling me about. This is concerning.

From: Melissa Ortiz <melissa.ortiz@unisco.com>
Sent: Tuesday, September 9, 2025 6:23 PM
To: Michael Deller <mdeller@teamready.com>
Cc: comeready.bp@unisco.com; Alfred Garcia <alfred.garcia@item.com>; Steven Garcia <steven.garcia@unisco.com>; Mark Golding <mark.golding@unisco.com>
Subject: [External] COME READY OPEN ORDERS 9/9

Hi Michael,
Please see below for updates team is working on getting the remaining orders released and shipped. We are still working on the list of orders that need to be canceled. The team is still working on putting back the freight so I can proceed to cancel. Items containing bottles are still giving the team issues but we are working closely with IT to get these updated ASAP.

Thanks 😊

Best regards,
Melissa Ortiz
